WEBVTT

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:07.490
Hane-senpai, wh-what did you just say?

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:08.500
Huh?

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:12.110
I just said I've never fallen off my bike before.

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:14.020
N-No way.

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:17.860
Now that I think about it, I've never seen her fall.

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:19.200
Have you fallen, Onsa-chan?

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:21.150
Of course I have.

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:25.000
You aren't a real biker
until you fall at least once.

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:40.440
What's that?

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.860
It's nice, isn't it?

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:44.090
If you clamp the front and back down,

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:47.200
the wind can't blow the cover off.

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:53.860
There we go.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:58.620
Huh?

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:24.270
この坂を上り切ったら
kono saka o noborikittara

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:28.230
必ず見える景色が好きだって
kanarazu mieru keshiki ga suki datte

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:28.270
必ず見える景色が好きだって

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:34.400
背中に羽を持つあの子も言って笑ってた
senaka ni hane o motsu ano ko mo itte waratteta

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:38.070
ドキドキが一瞬で
dokidoki ga isshun de

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:42.160
トキメキになっていくんだなんて
tokimeki ni natteikunda nante

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:45.870
あの頃は信じられなくて
ano koro wa shinjirarenakute

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:50.840
ただ見惚れていたよ
tada mitoreteita yo

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:55.470
このスピードに乗せた体温が
kono supiido ni noseta taion ga

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:59.220
今全身で伝う　通じ合う
ima zenshin de tsutau tsuujiau

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:02.850
物語の鍵はこの手に
monogatari no kagi wa kono te ni

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:06.350
ぎゅっと強く握っているから
gyutto tsuyoku nigitteiru kara

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:10.060
感じて　応えて　風になる
kanjite kotaete kaze ni naru

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:13.730
空に溶けて海を抱きしめる
sora ni tokete umi o dakishimeru

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:17.650
新しい世界が見えるはず
atarashii sekai ga mieru hazu

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:24.740
さぁ確かめに行ってみよう
saa tashikame ni ittemiyou

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:35.050
Nicoichi Motors

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:37.260
A World of What-ifs!!
Episode 12

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:39.010
I see, I see.
Your bike finally fell over?
A World of What-ifs!!
Episode 12

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:40.890
I see, I see.
Your bike finally fell over?

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.300
You're officially a real biker now.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:46.060
I hope my bike's okay.

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:50.270
The tank got a few scratches.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:53.520
But don't worry, this isn't anything we can't fix.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:54.360
Really?

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:55.530
Yeah.

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:57.490
Bring the bike inside.

00:02:57.490 --> 00:02:58.490
Let's get it fixed.

00:02:58.490 --> 00:02:59.860
Okay!

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:02.700
Ready, and...

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:09.040
Damn! We should've taken the gas out...

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:12.290
Even if we could, it's too late now!

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:12.710
Hane, put it on that tire.
Even if we could, it's too late now!

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:15.170
Hane, put it on that tire.

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:16.500
Right.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:19.050
And... go!

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:29.850
CV? You mean that pink 400?

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:31.140
Yeah.

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:34.520
We didn't carry it right and
we ended up denting it.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:37.780
So I was wondering the shop's
insurance could cover it.

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:40.030
We're painting the whole thing, anyway.

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:42.200
A used tank ought to be good enough.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.320
I guess, but...

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:47.740
It's not that easy to find
an undamaged tank, is it?

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:50.410
Actually, I have one.

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:55.250
A parts donor got me a tank
that came from a training bike.

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:02.090
Baita?

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:04.890
What happened? You're just a tank now!

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:16.110
I knew it was you!

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:18.610
What, are you embarrassed?

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:21.530
Look at you, turning away
as if you don't know me!

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:24.700
Fine, fine, I get it!

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:28.120
I didn't want to be seen like this.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:30.410
How did you end up here?

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:32.870
I retired from the training center,

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:35.960
then someone bought me and
drove me on the roads for a while.

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:38.710
But I got rammed from behind,
and they scrapped me.

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:41.840
My tank was unharmed, thanks to the guard.

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:45.340
Wow, that must have been rough.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:48.760
But you can still talk, even though
only your tank is left, huh?

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:51.930
Souls can exist in anything.

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:57.100
Although I can't keep up my tranny
identity without my neutered engine.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:00.530
I'm happy to see you again though, Baita.

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:06.110
You can't maintain your energy
in your current state?

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:07.870
That's not good.

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:10.030
Disturbing!

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:12.870
Ah, so she's just like you.

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:17.420
You talk to your bike a lot, too.

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:18.790
I-It's different!

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:22.170
I do it for show. It's acting.

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:24.840
It makes me look cooler.

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:27.130
I don't do it when no one's watching.

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:29.550
That's actually pretty uncool.

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:33.470
Hane-chan, just keep one thing in mind.

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:34.560
What?

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:37.770
You're making a big mistake if you think

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.980
bikes think in human terms.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:43.360
Bikes don't really want to run.

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:46.400
We want to be on our sides, sleeping.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:49.660
But humans keep us up, so we
have no choice but to stay up.

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:53.740
We run because humans make us.

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:58.210
So please, don't ever say things to a bike

00:05:58.210 --> 00:06:00.210
like, "You want to ride more, huh?"

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:03.630
Nothing could be more embarrassing.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:06.920
So please don't say it. Please<i> don't say it!</i>

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:11.350
I talk too much for a bike.

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:18.270
Baita...

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:22.110
You want to ride more, huh?

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:22.980
Nicoichi Motors

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:24.610
All right, it's done!
Nicoichi Motors

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:24.650
Nicoichi Motors

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:28.030
We painted it pearl pink, of course.

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:30.910
Wow, that's a nice paint job.

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:32.950
You put on decals, too.

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:34.540
Wicked!

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:36.950
It's back to normal again.

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:40.920
You're the perfect color now, Baita.

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:44.210
All right, Hane, let's test it out!

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:45.630
Yeah!

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:58.310
You guys!

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:00.560
We just got the tank fixed.

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:02.690
Of course I'm not letting it get another scratch!

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:04.110
Thank goodness.

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:07.490
I won't ever let you fall over again, Baita!

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:09.990
Idiot! Don't let go!

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:11.110
Ba
kuon<i>!!
Idiot! Don't let go!</i>

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:12.030
kuon<i>!!
Ba</i>

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:16.080
Ba
kuon<i>!!</i>

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:28.010
Look, it's a pack of Super Cubs!

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:31.380
Evening paper deliverers and mail carriers.

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:33.390
Super Cubs, you say?

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:36.060
Look closer. The two in front are Yamaha Mates.

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:36.390
YAMAHA MATE

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:39.680
The two behind them are
four-stroke Suzuki Birdies.

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:39.930
4-STROKE SUZUKI BIRDIE

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:43.270
The two farther back are the discontinued
two-stroke Suzuki Birdies.

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:44.440
2-STROKE SUZUKI BIRDIE

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:46.860
Finally, those are Suzuki Super Frees,
the predecessor to the Birdie.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:48.820
SUZUKI SUPER FREE

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:48.860
Finally, those are Suzuki Super Frees,
the predecessor to the Birdie.

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:51.280
I had no idea.

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:59.580
Among the bikes in the pack,
I am surprised there weren't any Super Cubs.

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:01.830
I hate to admit it,

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:06.630
but it's true that the Super Cub
influenced the design of business bikes.

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:09.590
The Suzuki Birdie is an original design, though.

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:11.420
Speaking of Super Cubs,

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:14.050
there's a famous story about how it was created.

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:16.100
Oh? What kind of story?

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:19.010
That thing about Honda's
founder, Honda Soichiro,

00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:21.430
and Executive Director Fujisawa Takeo, right?

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:23.560
Behold, Director!

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:26.440
The Super Cub prototype is complete!

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:28.070
Isn't it magnificent?

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:30.820
It's exactly the product that you wanted.

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:33.360
How many of these do you think we'll sell?

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:36.280
Yeah, Boss, this looks good.

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:38.280
This will sell without a doubt.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:39.910
We can bet on 30,000, at least.

00:08:39.910 --> 00:08:41.950
30,000 units a year?

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:43.830
No, I think we can do better.

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:47.130
Hang on, I think you're mistaken.

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:49.590
When I say 30,000...

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:51.340
I mean per month.

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:59.430
I never thought I'd see the day high
school girls imitate Honda Soichiro.

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:02.560
It's good to live a long life.

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:07.270
I swear...

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:12.030
If they weren't any bikes, the
world would go nowhere.

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:16.740
I wonder if bikes will disappear
some day, just like pagers did.

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:18.530
Don't worry.

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:20.740
Humanity won't ever become that smart.

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:24.160
Basically, bikes will always be around.

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:27.120
If all goes well, and your shop

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:29.960
sells lots more bikes, right, Onsa-senpai?

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:31.500
Even so,

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:34.300
you really don't know much about bikes, Hane.

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:35.760
I don't need to.

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:38.970
As long as I can ride my bike,
that's more than enough for me!

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:55.400
There's a new one for women.

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:58.610
What have you been reading?

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:04.870
It's hard to resist an article about the Katana, huh.

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:09.460
Every magazine has a Katana article regularly.

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:11.420
And every time...

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:15.880
Papa's Yoshimura 1135R has
a ten-page feature article.

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:20.220
So why does my Katana 400 only get 5 lines?!

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:22.390
Also, must they start it with

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:25.600
"the Katana 400 is often accused
of being a copy of a larger Katana"

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:27.770
They don't need to mention that!

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:32.570
Relax. There's only seven lines
about the Katana 250, too.

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:34.610
So, are you buying?

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:37.780
I am.

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:39.990
I'm buying this one, too.

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:41.070
Okay.

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:42.160
Huh?

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:43.700
What's this?

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:45.580
I've seen your face before!

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:47.620
Oh, it's you.

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:49.540
Hey, that's VIBE!
TL Note: VIBE is a parody of VIBES, an adult monthly magazine

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:51.960
I thought it was a bike magazine for women,

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:54.960
since there's always a woman on the cover.

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:57.300
But when I opened it, I was surprised!

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:58.300
Look!

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:00.550
In the middle is a pinup!

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:05.390
I don't know why, but there's a
naked woman on a motorcycle!

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:08.310
Did you know about this?

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:10.560
You know, we're at the cashier...

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:12.690
Look, you can see her pubes!

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:13.650
Her pubes!

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:18.610
How will you be paying?

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:19.700
Debit card, please.

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:24.490
Wait, what book did you just buy?

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:25.870
Western economics.

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:28.950
By the way, Sakura Hane,

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:35.170
what would you do if bikes were
to disappear from this world?

00:11:56.770 --> 00:11:58.190
Huh?

00:11:58.190 --> 00:12:00.440
When did I fall asleep?

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:03.490
I'm going to be late!

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:04.780
Huh?

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:06.160
I can't find it!

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:08.540
What's wrong, Onee-chan?

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:10.370
I can't find my helmet.

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:12.870
I always leave it here.

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:15.630
Oh, your helmet was dirty,

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:17.290
so I cleaned it for you.

00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:19.590
Here.

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:23.380
Jeez, that's a bicycle helmet!

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:27.810
Not that kind. It's more round
and sturdy, and it has a visor.

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:29.180
This one, then?

00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:31.060
Not even close!

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:47.030
Is it just me, or are there
a lot of bicycles today?

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:48.030
Oh, Hane.

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:52.080
What's up? You aren't biking today?

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:54.210
Nevermind that!

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:56.540
I can't find my helmet.

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:59.460
Wait, what about you?

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:01.380
You're riding a bike!

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:03.470
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:05.130
I do this every day.

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:07.510
What are you guys doing?

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:08.890
You're going to be late.

00:13:08.890 --> 00:13:10.390
Et tu, Rin-chan?

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:11.970
Isn't it strange?

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:14.310
Why are you all bicycling to school?

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:16.650
What are you talking about, Hane?

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:19.270
You always bicycle to school, too.

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:20.610
What are you talking about?!

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:23.150
I've always ridden a motorcycle to school!

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:24.780
"Motorcycle"?

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:25.610
What's that?

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:29.280
Huh? But you just called it a "bike."

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:33.250
Oh, by bike you mean bicycle?

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:36.330
Huh?! I mean motorcycles!

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:38.920
I bought a book yesterday, remember?

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:40.090
See!

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:44.050
Ladies.. cycle...

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:46.840
I get it now.

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:51.060
I don't know the reason,

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:55.890
but I somehow got into a world
without motorcyclces!
The best lube to keep
your groin from chafing!
The best lube to keep
your groin from chafing!

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:58.060
Seriously, though, your bike's so old.
The best lube to keep
your groin from chafing!
The best lube to keep
your groin from chafing!

00:13:58.060 --> 00:13:59.810
Seriously, though, your bike's so old.

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:03.820
You're still riding that thing?
It's a hand-me-down, right?

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:06.610
You just don't get it, Shaggy!

00:14:06.610 --> 00:14:07.780
Look at this.

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:12.950
The beautiful curves on
these semi-drop handlebars!

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:16.210
These unique, star-shaped aluminum wheels!

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:20.750
It's the awesomeest bicycle in
the history of bicycles!

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:23.630
It's the Suzuki Sky Young!

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:26.630
Wow, Rin-chan hasn't changed.

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:31.010
Those wheels have the same shape as her Katana!

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:34.100
Hey, how's everyone else?

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:35.180
Everyone else?

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:36.680
Like Hijiri-chan.

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:39.020
Oh, Hijiri?

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:41.690
She just arrived.

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:48.700
Good morning, everyone!

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:51.160
I've installed a Delae S

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:54.870
on my Colnago Ferrari today!

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:57.160
Nice! Congrats!

00:14:57.160 --> 00:14:58.830
Thank you!

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:01.670
So Hijiri-chan doesn't ride bicycles?

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:04.420
Nope, just setting them up and polishing them.

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:06.710
Then what's Chisame-chan doing?

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:08.340
What else?

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:11.340
She's doing her morning training.

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:15.680
She's the daughter of the professional
bike racer Nakano, after all.

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:19.060
Oh, so she becomes the Nakano of <i>that</i> sport.

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:22.730
I think I'm starting to enjoy this.

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:26.110
Then what does Raimu-senpai ride?

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:27.570
Lime?

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:29.190
Do you know who that is, Rin?

00:15:29.190 --> 00:15:31.490
I've never heard that name.

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:32.950
I see.

00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:35.870
I guess there's no Raimu-senpai

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:38.200
in a world without motorcycles.

00:15:44.710 --> 00:15:48.210
Sorry to make you walk with me, guys.

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:50.470
Nah, it's nice every once in a while.

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:54.390
If I just biked all the time, I'd get bad at walking.

00:15:57.010 --> 00:15:58.140
I get it!

00:15:58.970 --> 00:16:03.060
Everyone used to talk about how
little I know about motorcycles,

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:05.400
but it's the other way around in this world.

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:07.860
I'm the only one who knows.

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:10.610
If they don't remember
anything about motorcycles,

00:16:10.610 --> 00:16:13.740
then I can teach them!

00:16:14.530 --> 00:16:16.530
Hey, guys, listen to this!

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:20.000
I just came up with an amazing idea!

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:20.790
Huh?

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:21.620
What?

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:23.870
Hey, you know what?

00:16:23.870 --> 00:16:27.170
How about we put a car engine on a bicycle?

00:16:27.590 --> 00:16:30.920
Then it'll move on its own,
and it'll be easy to get up hills!

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:32.670
We'll call it an "auto-bi!"

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:34.840
Good idea, right?

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:39.720
What are you talking about? That's crazy.

00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:44.190
I've always thought you're
weird, but not <i>that</i> weird.

00:16:44.190 --> 00:16:47.270
So this is Hane-senpai in normal mode.

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:49.610
Huh?

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:52.280
Biking is a sport.

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:56.160
If you want to get around easily,
you can just drive a car.

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:57.370
A Suzuki compact!

00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:03.250
Besides, Hane, engines are
super heavy, you know.

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:04.920
Like, a hundred kilograms!
TL Note: A lot of pounds

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:08.460
It'd make more sense to
put one on a four-wheeler.

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:11.670
They're working on collision safety and

00:17:11.670 --> 00:17:13.920
pedestrian protection for cars now.

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:18.430
I bet your "auto-bi" doesn't
have a seatbelt, either!

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:19.930
That's dangerous.

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:23.520
And what's with "auto-bi"?

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:26.020
What happened to the "ke" in bike?

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:29.150
I guess that's just Hane being Hane.

00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:30.570
Huh?

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:34.530
Uh... Well, what do you think, Chisame-chan?

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:39.070
I don't think that "auto-bi" thing could work.

00:17:39.070 --> 00:17:41.740
There've been fewer car accidents since

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:43.620
bicycle lanes were finally added.

00:17:43.950 --> 00:17:46.670
There's no way a third class of vehicle

00:17:46.670 --> 00:17:50.090
that's neither a bicycle nor a car
would be approved now.

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:51.590
Aww, but...

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:53.010
Although...

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:56.760
In a hypothetical world,

00:17:56.760 --> 00:17:57.720
what if,

00:17:57.970 --> 00:18:01.510
the founder of Honda, Honda Soichiro,

00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:04.060
made a vehicle for the masses,

00:18:04.060 --> 00:18:07.020
not by putting an engine on the Daihachi,

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:09.350
but on a bicycle, instead?

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:13.280
History may have changed.
Honda might not have become a minivan company,

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:18.320
but rather, your so-called "auto-bi" company.

00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:19.910
But it is!

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:22.740
Honda <i>does</i> make motorcycles!

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:25.450
Speaking of the original Odyssey,

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:27.580
there's that famous story about its inception.

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:32.840
Oh, that thing about Honda Soichiro and
Executive Director Fujisawa Takeo, right?

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:33.750
I got this.

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:37.130
30,000 units a month, right?

00:18:38.430 --> 00:18:41.890
I didn't think Hane would know about that.

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:49.850
Good day, everyone!

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:55.230
I know.

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:58.030
We were all riding motorcycles.

00:18:58.450 --> 00:19:00.490
I do know!

00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:03.740
Smarten up, Hane.

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:07.580
Only superior people can ride bicycles.

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:12.790
Only idiots ride motorcycles.

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:18.050
That was a million-yen road bike!

00:19:18.050 --> 00:19:18.970
What should we do?

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:20.760
We're going after it, obviously!

00:19:20.760 --> 00:19:23.640
All right, I'm going to pass
it on my 100,000-yen bike!

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:25.470
Go, Sky Young!

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:36.270
I see.

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:38.820
Everyone got smarter.

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:42.910
For convenience, there's cars,

00:19:42.910 --> 00:19:45.740
and for using your own power, there's bicycles.

00:19:45.740 --> 00:19:50.290
There are separate lanes for
people, cars, and bicycles.

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:52.040
There are fewer accidents.

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:55.250
It looks like things are running a lot smoother.

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:57.130
But...

00:19:57.130 --> 00:20:01.380
But, a world without motorcycles

00:20:01.380 --> 00:20:03.930
is just a little bit lonely.

00:20:09.980 --> 00:20:11.390
Clank.

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:13.520
Kickstand, check.

00:20:13.520 --> 00:20:14.860
Click.

00:20:15.360 --> 00:20:16.940
Prrrrrr.

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:18.480
Vroom.

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:20.190
Release the clutch.

00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:22.570
Shift to first gear. Click.

00:20:22.570 --> 00:20:24.910
Right turn signal on.

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:27.410
Shoulder check, done.

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:30.080
Sakura Hane, ready to go.

00:20:30.450 --> 00:20:35.210
Vroooooom.

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:38.800
Zoom!

00:21:11.660 --> 00:21:12.790
Everyone...

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:14.540
You're late, Hane.

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:17.630
You didn't forgot our touring today, right?

00:21:17.630 --> 00:21:19.920
Oh, my. You're still in your pajamas.

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:39.480
Morning, Hane-chan.

00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:41.480
Baita!

00:21:42.030 --> 00:21:44.990
Sorry, I had a weird dream,

00:21:44.990 --> 00:21:46.280
and I overslept.

00:21:46.280 --> 00:21:47.740
Jeez.

00:21:47.740 --> 00:21:50.410
What kind of dream was it?

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:51.700
Well...

00:21:51.700 --> 00:21:55.210
Onee-chan, I polished your helmet for you.

00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:57.460
Thanks, Yume!

